# L §7.3: "pow(x, q) with a non-integer q" needs to u; "pow(x, n) with an integer n is exact" (§7.1).  A power
# read from a row is an integer here: exact, 2^3 = 8; a non-integer power without to is refused LOAD-TO (found at
# run: the whole reality is refused, L §8.3).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input two: num
input three: num
def p: num = pow(two, three) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  two = 2
  three = 3

ask a: p law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: 8
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
